#! ia 1.0

@capability operation-method
  meaning
    says "Work with operation records under the IA methodology: the operation-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an operation. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an operation?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook operation-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook operation-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with operation records, each a declared operation bound to an implementation, input, output and effect contract that the host installs: orient through ia position --word operation and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with operation records?"
  subject
    subject-word operation
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word operation at the seat the work concerns, read the operation records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary operation --schema for the sections and fields an operation carries."
      Inference means "Read the operation's implementation, inputs, outputs and effects."
      Decision means "operation is a word of authoring-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/authoring-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these operation records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the operation must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "State the inputs, outputs and effects the operation needs, and the implementation the host installs for it."
      Decision means "Extend an existing operation through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the operation will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the operation; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the operation's contract; installing its implementation stays with the host."
      Decision means "Change operation records only through ia preview operation <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that the declared effects match what the implementation does when it runs."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the operation, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability authoring-guide-method
  meaning
    says "Work with authoring-guide records under the IA methodology: the authoring-guide-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an authoring-guide. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an authoring-guide?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook authoring-guide-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook authoring-guide-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with authoring-guide records, each a vocabulary owner and schema associated with an authoring reference and usage guidance: orient through ia position --word authoring-guide and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with authoring-guide records?"
  subject
    subject-word authoring-guide
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word authoring-guide at the seat the work concerns, read the authoring-guide records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary authoring-guide --schema for the sections and fields an authoring-guide carries."
      Inference means "Read the guide for the word: its owner, schema and reference."
      Decision means "authoring-guide is a word of authoring-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/authoring-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these authoring-guide records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the authoring-guide must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide what guidance authors of the word need, citing its schema rather than copying it."
      Decision means "Extend an existing authoring-guide through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the authoring-guide will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the authoring-guide; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the guide with its owner, schema and reference."
      Decision means "Change authoring-guide records only through ia preview authoring-guide <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that the guide still matches the schema ia vocabulary <word> --schema shows."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the authoring-guide, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
